# Git-crypt encrypted files. This repo is public.
#
# Files matching the patterns below are encrypted on commit and decrypted on
# checkout by the official git-crypt (Andrew Ayer's, `pacman -S git-crypt`).
# The repo's symmetric key is in pass at
# `hosts/desktop/dotfiles-git-crypt-key-official` (base64 of
# `git-crypt export-key`), and Stephen's GPG key is a git-crypt user
# (.git-crypt/keys/), so either unlocks it.
#
# `shell/.postinstall` unlocks a fresh clone from pass. To unlock by hand,
# from a clean working tree:
#
#   with your GPG key:   cd ~/.dotfiles && git-crypt unlock
#   with the pass key:   key=$(mktemp -p "$XDG_RUNTIME_DIR") \
#                          && pass show hosts/desktop/dotfiles-git-crypt-key-official | base64 -d > "$key" \
#                          && git-crypt unlock "$key"; shred -u "$key"
#
# Until unlocked, git-crypt's filter is not configured and git would commit a
# matching file in plaintext: the .githooks/pre-commit gate refuses that, and
# `./dotfiles check-crypt` checks every committed one.

*.env filter=git-crypt diff=git-crypt
